{"cluster_id": "C-3430", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B017-023"], "canonical_claim": "`cas_blob_meta` uses `Never` compression, so its stored bytes are the text itself and `blobMetaKey` remains unchanged without a `.zst` suffix.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase4-blob-meta.md#global-constraints"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3431", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B017-059", "B038-014"], "canonical_claim": "Manifest keys migrate from `.proto` to the `Always` `.zst` suffix, `parseManifestKey` strips `.zst`, and persistence actually applies `sealObject` and `openObject`.; Part manifests are stored under `cas/manifests/<ns>/<epoch-hex>-<seq-hex>/<ordinal>.zst`, blob envelopes use `CasLayout::blobKey`, blob freshness sidecars use `CasLayout::blobMetaKey`, and GC source-edge runs use `gc/gen/<g>/\u2026\u200b/runs`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase6-manifest-stream.md#cruxes", "src/Disks/DiskObjectStorage/MetadataStorages/ContentAddressed/Formats/README.md#bucket-map"]}
