{"cluster_id": "C-3437", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B019-131"], "canonical_claim": "Local disks are durable at `renameParts`, plain upstream S3 defers local metadata including tmp-to-final rename until disk commit, and post-`39cf3279652` CA deferred blobs, manifest, and ref publication until disk commit.", "issue_ids": ["39cf3279652"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-17-part-durability-before-keeper-commit-design.md#L31-L35"]}
