{"cluster_id": "C-3440", "topic": "namespace life object layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B027-033", "B028-003", "B028-017", "B030-024", "B032-002"], "canonical_claim": "Life-owned physical keys use the opaque-life layout `cas/ns/stream/<life_id>/_log/<txn>`, `cas/ns/stream/<life_id>/_snap/<txn>`, `cas/ns/state/<life_id>/_ckpt`, and `cas/ns/state/<life_id>/_files/<relative-name>`. Additionally, The final namespace-owned layout uses immutable stream objects under `cas/ns/stream/<life_id>/{_log,_snap,_cleanup}` and point/path-addressed state under `cas/ns/state/<life_id>/{_ckpt,_files}`; `_cleanup` is transitional and is removed by the removal lifecycle. Additionally, The final physical key grammar is `cas/ns/stream/<life_id>/_log/<txn>.zst`, `cas/ns/stream/<life_id>/_snap/<txn>.zst`, `cas/ns/state/<life_id>/_ckpt.zst`, and `cas/ns/state/<life_id>/_files/<relative-name>`; the transitional `cas/ns/stream/<life_id>/_cleanup/<txn>` family is removed by Task 5. Additionally, Namespace files are stored as direct objects under `cas/ns/state/<life_id>/_files/<relative-name>`, with the builder using the incarnation from `NamespaceLifeId`; `roots/` contains only loose mountpoint objects outside catalog ownership. Additionally, The namespace-file key shape is `cas/ns/state/<life_id>/_files/<relative-name>`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/2026-08-02-r1-verbatim-file-aliasing-closure.md#unqualified-namespace-file-keys", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#task-4d", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#invariants", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-29-cas-stage-b-namespace-life-amendments.md#incarnation-key-namespace-files"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3441", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B028-002", "B028-052", "B030-040", "B030-044", "B030-128", "B032-001", "B032-030"], "canonical_claim": "Namespace-file rebirth safety is closed by keys of the form `cas/ns/state/<life_id>/_files/<relative-name>` and by binding reads and delayed writes to the exact `NamespaceLifeId` selected before rebirth.; Every namespace-file API accepts `NamespaceLifeId`; hot reads and writes use an already-held life handle without a catalog GET, and delayed write callbacks capture the exact incarnation present at admission. Additionally, Incarnation qualification must not move namespace files into the ref log or add catalog reads, ref-log appends, blob uploads, folder-manifest rewrites, or changes to direct-object backend request counts on the namespace-file path. Additionally, The Stage B namespace-file change must preserve the current direct-object implementation and must not change `MergeTreeDeduplicationLog` or move namespace files into the ref log.; CAS namespace files are keyed by an opaque `NamespaceLifeId`, so debris from one namespace life cannot be addressed through a later life with the same namespace name.; At the plain-object, pool, and layout layers, namespace-file operations take an explicit `NamespaceLifeId`; `Layout::namespaceFileKey` and `namespaceFilesPrefix` have no namespace-only key helper.; The catalog entry's incarnation is the opaque physical `life_id` shared by the ref layer and namespace files; the logical `RootNamespace` remains in catalog entries and in-memory `NamespaceLifeId` values but is absent from life-owned object keys.", "issue_ids": ["R1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/2026-07-28-ref-rework-adjacent-findings.md#r1-verbatim-alias", "docs/superpowers/cas/2026-08-02-r1-verbatim-file-aliasing-closure.md#unqualified-namespace-file-keys", "docs/superpowers/cas/2026-08-02-stage-b-midpoint-audit.md#t6-6-namespace-file-apis-and-hot-path-catalog-gets", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#global-constraints", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-29-cas-stage-b-namespace-life-amendments.md#deduplication-performance-constraint", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-29-cas-stage-b-namespace-life-amendments.md#namespace-file-requirements"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3442", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B033-062", "B046-006", "B048-062"], "canonical_claim": "Persisted CAS object-storage format strings, including the serialization key `gen` and `_snap` and `_ckpt` object-name suffixes, are not renamed by the obscure-name cleanup.; The persisted CasFoldSealFormat fields named gen and the gtest_cas_fold_seal_format.cpp golden value ,\"gen\":\"7\" remain unchanged because they are part of the persisted format. Additionally, The persisted fold-seal serialization key `gen` remains unchanged in `Formats/CasFoldSealFormat.cpp` and its golden test; `gc/gen/*` is likewise a persisted object-key path, not a renameable user-facing abbreviation.", "issue_ids": ["T8"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-03-cas-obscure-names/t2-report.md#L3-L14", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-03-cas-obscure-names/t8-report.md#L3-L24", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-03-cas-obscure-names-cleanup.md#global-constraints"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3443", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B036-037", "B036-038"], "canonical_claim": "Incarnation monotonicity is required per `(ns,shard)`, not globally: incarnations may collide across different shards because the cursor key includes `(shard, incarnation)`.; A delete-and-recreate of the same `(ns,shard)` must draw an incarnation strictly greater than that path's high-water mark; reusing an incarnation on the same path causes an ABA error.", "issue_ids": ["D1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/CaGcShardIncarnationCore_RESULTS.md#conclusions"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3444", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B037-007"], "canonical_claim": "Fresh opaque life ids make residue from a dead life structurally inert; reusing a dead id can make a reborn life's first read reach predecessor bytes.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/CaRefCatalogCore_RESULTS.md#carefcatalogcore-lifecycle-properties"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3445", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B037-047"], "canonical_claim": "The exact `_ckpt.committed_through` frontier is the only durable authority for ref-log install, acknowledgement, successor allocation, snapshot publication, and seal publication.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/CaRefTableSnapshotLogCore_RESULTS.md#task-5b-exact-committed-frontier-extension"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3446", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B037-051"], "canonical_claim": "Seal publication consists of conditional creation of the immutable seal followed by a same-contribution checkpoint CAS that atomically advances `lastEpochSeal` and `committedThrough`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/CaRefTableSnapshotLogCore_RESULTS.md#task-5b-exact-committed-frontier-extension"]}
