{"cluster_id": "C-3450", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B038-011"], "canonical_claim": "`CasTextFormat.{h,cpp}` is the only code that knows the persisted CAS text-file shape.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["src/Disks/DiskObjectStorage/MetadataStorages/ContentAddressed/Formats/README.md#L1-L6"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3451", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B018-042", "B038-012", "B040-151"], "canonical_claim": "The CAS object inventory has no binary formats and no protobuf dependency; `cas_run` is sorted NDJSON read as a non-seekable stream with a whole-file seal checksum, while the part manifest is the single `PayloadHybrid` object with a text header, descriptor metadata, sorted entry records, `{\"n\":\u2026}` trailer, and banner-framed raw inline-payload zone.; v3 makes every metadata byte human-readable with head, zstdcat, jq, less, and diff; raw blob payload remains the only non-metadata binary region; The codecs-v3 audit concluded that all 15 live persisted CAS objects have text codecs under `Core/Formats/`, no `.proto` files remain, and both binary codecs were deleted.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/codecs_proposal_v3.md#design-goals", "docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-16-unattended-codecs-txn-sourcelayout-part1.md#L21-L40", "src/Disks/DiskObjectStorage/MetadataStorages/ContentAddressed/Formats/README.md#L1-L7"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3452", "topic": "storage layout", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B038-020"], "canonical_claim": "A CAS blob is immutable, shared, and keyed by a content digest; identity is established by re-hashing bytes, with no trust-the-checksum shortcut, and its freshness sidecar is `blobKey` plus `.meta`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["src/Disks/DiskObjectStorage/MetadataStorages/ContentAddressed/README.md#L1-L23"]}
